rect_records_2026-08-11 — the exact strided-rectangle borrow record
===================================================================

Branch      perf/rect-records, base 140f914 (PR #504 merged)
Host        Apple M4 Pro, 8P + 4E, macOS 26.5.2, aarch64
Toolchain   stable-aarch64-apple-darwin, no -C target-cpu=native
Harness     scripts/perf/tiled_wallcpu.sh under ~/bin/measlock, NEVER niced
Report      scripts/perf/rect_report.py (paired per-round ratios, round 0
            dropped as cold, whole rounds dropped when any arm saw a foreign
            process above 25% CPU)
Fit         total = a + b*frames at two frame counts per cell, so process
            startup / mmap / decoder construction drop out of wall AND CPU
Full write-up  docs/RECT_RECORDS.md

VERDICT
-------
NOT the default. The mechanism is exact, sound, live and correct; it is
-1.0%..-1.8% wall on 5 of 6 multi-tile t=8 cells, NULL on `c256x2048` t=8 (the
cell it was built for, 4/7 sign), and +1.26% at t=1 on `v4k8tile` (0/11 rounds
below 1.000) where the path is never taken and the only difference is code size.
It stays behind `--features __lf_rect`.

THE NUMBER THE ROUND EXISTS FOR
-------------------------------
A `LfBlock::fill` per-row registration costs 2.42-2.71 ns at the MARGIN, measured
by adding a duplicate per row in ONE binary (RAV1D_LF_DOUBLE, +180,434
registrations/frame, 0 of 25 rounds on the other side), against `c256x2048` t=8's
19.71 ns/registration AVERAGE. The decoder's largest registration site is 31.7%
of the population and 3.9-4.4% of the tracker's CPU. The cost tracks DISTINCT
SHARD LINES visited, not records filed.

ARMS (all verified to emit ONE md5 per (cell, threads) before any timing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
plain      HEAD default codegen: machinery present, rectangle path OFF
plainB     byte-identical copy of plain (same sha256) — the noise floor
plainC     SAME SOURCE as plain built in a second worktree — layout-only control
machoff    140f914's tracker source built in THIS tree
base       140f914's tracker source built in its own worktree
rect       --features __lf_rect
rect1      --features __lf_rect1 (one-shard rectangles only; 20.4% of fills)
dbloff/on  ONE binary (--features __probe_lf_hull), RAV1D_LF_DOUBLE off / on
untracked  --features probe-untracked (tracker-removed ceiling, bit-identical)
dav1d_fd1  dav1d 1.5.4 --framedelay 1

